Subject: [HW-08 / OS-04] Iris VPU5 balanced PM and error lifecycle

GPL-2.0-only; kernel-derived changes retain upstream file notices.

Consolidate debug6 revision 2's balanced power/clock/session lifecycle against
the reviewed 7.3.4 baseline, without the temporary debug4 register tracing.
Zero-OPP release remains a separate non-overlapping patch. The diagnostic
revision passed three controlled deep cycles including an open H.264 session;
this trace-free candidate still requires its own physical qualification.

Power ownership adapts the idempotent power-off reference:
https://github.com/CFM880/nabu-iris/commit/945e8b954027ab55f28edf92186df986f0802c02
The legacy WFI/PC_READY and secure-state handshake follows the Qualcomm Iris1
reference in docs/iris-driver-review.md. Keep failed cores in ERROR until full
teardown; serialize init/deinit, retain queues/firmware/sessions across PM, and
drain full teardown IRQs outside the core mutex. No automatic reset-on-open.

